From 2ec377b6994c88fc8e1d2e30153591c621c3d31d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 06:19:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 092/114] rust: drm: add private ioctl compat translations

Allow Rust DRM drivers to declare translations for pointer-bearing
private ioctls whose 32-bit layout differs from the native UAPI type.

Dispatch translated commands through drm_ioctl_kernel() so normal
DRM permission and unplug checks remain in force. Fall back to
drm_compat_ioctl() for core commands and private commands which need
no translation.

Keep the native driver table generated by declare_drm_ioctls! so
argument types and command numbers continue to come from the normal
generated UAPI bindings.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
